## Part 3 — Browser Game Technology Landscape

Modern web browsers are full-fledged application runtimes capable of near-native 3D graphics and complex physics.

### Technology Matrix & Evaluation

| Engine / Tech | 2D/3D Capability | Visual Fidelity | Performance / FPS | Mobile Compatibility | Load Time / Asset Size | PlayThorn Viability |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Unity WebGL (WASM)** | 2D & 3D (Console-grade) | ★★★★★ (High) | ★★★★☆ (60 FPS on GPU) | ★★★☆☆ (Requires RAM) | 10MB - 50MB (Brotli) | **Essential** (Top 3D Games) |
| **Godot 4 Web (WASM/WebGL2)**| 2D & 3D | ★★★★☆ (High) | ★★★★☆ (Smooth) | ★★★★☆ (Good) | 5MB - 20MB | **Essential** (Fastest growing indie engine) |
| **PlayCanvas** | 3D Focused | ★★★★★ (Photorealistic) | ★★★★★ (Web Native) | ★★★★★ (Excellent) | 2MB - 10MB | **High Priority** (Lightweight 3D) |
| **Three.js / Babylon.js** | Custom 3D JavaScript | ★★★★☆ (High) | ★★★★★ (Direct WebGL) | ★★★★★ (Excellent) | 1MB - 8MB | **High Priority** (Custom Web3D) |
| **Phaser 3 / PixiJS** | 2D Focused | ★★★☆☆ (Clean 2D) | ★★★★★ (120 FPS) | ★★★★★ (Flawless) | 500KB - 5MB | **Essential** (2D Arcade/Puzzle) |
| **Construct 3 / Defold** | 2D & Lite 3D | ★★★★☆ (Polished 2D) | ★★★★★ (Highly Optimized)| ★★★★★ (Flawless) | 1MB - 10MB | **Essential** (Hyper-Casual) |
| **WebGPU (Next-Gen)** | Next-Gen 3D Compute | ★★★★★+ (Ray-Tracing potential) | ★★★★★ (Low CPU Overhead) | ★★★☆☆ (Browser roll-out) | Varies | **Future-Proofing** (2026+ Standard) |

### Key Technical Requirement: Cross-Origin Isolation
Modern multithreaded Unity and Godot 4 WebGL builds require `SharedArrayBuffer`. To enable this in the browser, PlayThorn's backend/edge servers must serve:
```http
Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp (or credentialless)
```

