## Part 7 — 120-Point Game Quality Scoring System

Every game considered for PlayThorn must be evaluated against this weighted rubric:

$$\text{Total Score} = \sum (\text{Factor Score} \times \text{Weight})$$

| Evaluation Criteria | Weight | What We Look For |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Gameplay & Core Loop** | **20%** | Is it instantly fun? Does it have a clear "one more round" hook? |
| **Graphics & Visual Craft** | **18%** | High resolution assets, smooth 60 FPS rendering, polished UI design. |
| **Performance & Load Time** | **15%** | Initial load under 3 seconds on 4G connection; zero memory leaks. |
| **Mobile & Touch UX** | **15%** | Responsive touch controls, correct orientation locks, no UI clipping. |
| **Retention & Progression** | **12%** | LocalStorage / Cloud save capability, unlockables, high score leaderboards. |
| **Licensing & Ownership** | **10%** | Clear legal commercial rights (self-hosted or verified developer partnership). |
| **Sound & Audio Polish** | **10%** | High-quality audio effects and soundtrack with toggle controls. |

*Passing Threshold*: **Minimum 75/100 Total Score** required to be published on PlayThorn.

