## Part 9 — Technical Architecture for Multi-Engine Browser Platform

PlayThorn's Next.js 15 App Router architecture will be upgraded to support dynamic, multi-engine game containers.

### Container Architecture Diagram

```mermaid
graph TD
    UserClient[User Browser] --> NextRouter[Next.js 15 App Router /game/slug]
    NextRouter --> EngineDetector{Engine Type?}
    
    EngineDetector -->|Self-Hosted OpenSource| WebGLContainer[Native WASM/WebGL Canvas Container]
    EngineDetector -->|Unity / Godot 4| SharedArrayBufferContainer[Cross-Origin Isolated SharedArrayBuffer IFrame]
    EngineDetector -->|Publisher Network| SandboxedIFrame[Secure Sandboxed IFrame Container]
    
    WebGLContainer --> CDN[PlayThorn Asset CDN]
    SharedArrayBufferContainer --> ServiceWorker[PlayThorn PWA Cache & Asset Preloader]
    SandboxedIFrame --> ExternalCDN[Authorized Publisher CDN]
```

### Frontend Implementation Specs (`src/components/GameContainer.tsx`)
1. **Dynamic Aspect Ratio Viewport**: Auto-resizes between 16:9, 4:3, and 9:16 portrait modes with full-screen API support.
2. **PWA Asset Preloading**: Pre-fetches high-frequency WebGL assets using background web workers so games launch instantaneously.
3. **Cross-Origin Opener Policy**: Dynamically injects security headers when hosting Godot 4 and Unity 2023+ multithreaded WASM builds.

